direct-tail-defer
owner: opus-5 session 53f400ad
started: 2026-09-16
what: operator's ask (2026-09-16): mutual recursion in a direct block
  should need no word. Today `else isOdd(n - 1)` (coloured, or marked
  with ! / .reflect) COMPILES, answers at small n, and overflows the
  stack at depth — the worst failure mode. The rule: defer a call in
  TAIL POSITION of the block whose type is the block's program type,
  in addition to today's self-call rule; a call already wrapped in
  tailcall/delay/defer is left alone so the explicit spelling does not
  pay twice. Cost to measure: one Delay per tail-position program call
  that is not recursive. Eager is excluded (construction evaluates
  there by design). Failing test FIRST.
files: src/main/scala/Direct.scala, src/test/scala/TestDirectDeep.scala,
  docs/direct-style.md, docs/theory/08-direct-style.md,
  specs/direct-macro.md, BACKLOG.md, CHANGELOG.md
